      "comment": "Latin has no noun for a compromise; it says what each side does. When both give way, <span lang=\"la\">uterque aliquid dē suō remittit</span>; the terms agreed are a <span lang=\"la\">condiciō</span> or <span lang=\"la\">pactum</span> (see agreement)."
    },
